Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:32:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(files): a Save As name without its extension gets it

On Linux the desktop's Save dialog (GTK's file chooser) hands the name
back as typed: "cabinet" was saved as "cabinet", a valid document the
Open dialog's "Supported files" filter then hid. Windows and macOS add
the filter's extension in the dialog, so only Linux saw it. A name
without one of the type's extensions now gets the type's first
(withExtension: cabinet -> cabinet.shz, cabinet.v2 -> cabinet.v2.shz,
part -> part.stl; Cabinet.SHZ stays). The shell accepts such a path as
the chosen one less its added extension (without_added_extension in
sawhorse-safe-save) and then allows it by its full name, so the saves
and reads that follow go by it.

Tests: save.test.ts (the dialog's name with and without the extension,
in either case; a cancelled dialog; a second save to the handle's
path), safe-save (the chosen path less its added extension; none to
take off).

Found on Linux (the 0.1.0-alpha.4 .deb) by scripting the app under Xvfb.

